# Statistics over a list of numbers. Pure folds, identical on every backend. Integer results: `mean` truncates, and `total` of an empty list is zero. `least` / `greatest` assume a non-empty list. `variance` and `standard-deviation` need floats and live in a float-stats follow-up.

load @term/seed/code/list
  find list

task total
  take values, like list
  like number
  save out, code 0
  walk list
    read values
    hook next
      take site, name item
      save out
        call add
          read out
          read item
  send back, read out

task mean
  take values, like list
  like number
  fork test
    hook test
      call is-equal
        read values/length
        code 0
    hook hold
      send back, code 0
    hook miss
      send back
        call divide
          call total
            read values
          read values/length

task least
  take values, like list
  like number
  save best
    call values/at
      code 0
  walk list
    read values
    hook next
      take site, name item
      fork test
        hook test
          call is-below
            read item
            read best
        hook hold
          save best, read item
  send back, read best

task greatest
  take values, like list
  like number
  save best
    call values/at
      code 0
  walk list
    read values
    hook next
      take site, name item
      fork test
        hook test
          call is-above
            read item
            read best
        hook hold
          save best, read item
  send back, read best

task span
  take values, like list
  like number
  send back
    call subtract
      call greatest
        read values
      call least
        read values
